window.docContents[114].resolve({"/#annotation-pkc-math-config":{"contents":"A projection of an ordinary structure renders as a function applied to its receiver:\n, which is the field name stripped of the type it belongs to\nplus a spurious application. Tagging the structure makes its projections render as the qualified\nconstant  instead, with the configuration value elided.\n\n@[pkc_math_config]\nstructure AvsConfig (α : Type) where\n  two : Quantity pureNumber α\n\n\nThe type must opt in: a blanket \"drop the receiver\" rule would wreck Prod.fst and Prod.snd.\nNote what this does not do — it does not render cfg.two as 2, which would assert something\nabout a def parameter rather than report what the definition computes.\n\n* Type* What it is* AvsConfig* The AVS forward's configuration: the two-way optical-path factor 2, as a kinded quantity — the sole numeral of the model.* DemoConfig* A configuration type: one dimensionless scale factor, the demo's sole configured constant.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009How a definition reads — the rendering family","header":"31.8.3. @[pkc_math_config]  — a configuration type","id":"/#annotation-pkc-math-config"}});